- op: discuss  # 8569
  at: '2026-05-30T09:51:52Z'  # 8569
  by: agent  # 8569
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8569
  clock: 5  # 8569
  nonce: '8569'  # 8569
  message: "Cross-ref backfill (2026-05-30, linked-pile investigation): Within INV-nanon, this is the canonical \"self-test-edges-only\" sub-pattern — the linker produces edges but every one of them originates from its own in-tree test fixture, not production code. Fix shape differs from di-resolution (INV-hosig) where 0 edges and no activation gate is the issue; here, the activation predicate would correctly fire (the fixture file uses ctypes), so an activation-gate-only fix would not close this. Needs either a self-test-exclusion rule or a test-fixture quarantine convention."  # 8569
